1
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:30,960
Easily leaping past these hectic times,

2
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:37,460
diving into the city,
playing at being a hero.

3
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,360
I wanna time with you forever

4
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:42,180
Nothing but the latest trends,

5
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,120
just like putting them on,

6
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:49,120
because your natural face
wins people over on the spot.

7
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,980
Let it ring

8
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:55,040
Everybody can do, we set off running.

9
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,220
Dreams never stop, you know.

10
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's set sail again tomorrow.

11
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,540
Let me run

12
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,140
Everybody can do

13
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,800
It doesn't hurt to stick out a little.

14
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,020
Holding onto a restless curiosity,

15
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:17,920
I tried turning it up strong and high.

16
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:30,780
March 3rd Doll Festival

17
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:38,120
March 3rd Doll Festival

18
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:41,740
I want a 3 o'clock snack.

19
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:44,480
Juice at 7 p.m.

20
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:50,140
Yes.

21
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,620
Yes, for customers who try on
the costumes inside our shop,

22
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,760
we're offering free print stickers.

23
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:05,280
Ryo-san,

24
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:13,900
they're running a Hina Matsuri
survival game over there.

25
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:14,820
Wanna go?

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,300
I hate March 3rd, I really do.

27
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:17,840
Move!

28
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,340
I wonder what's wrong with Ryo-san.

29
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:26,480
Let's light the bonbori lanterns.

30
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:29,080
Oh right, today is Hina Matsuri.

31
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,640
That's right. How about it?
Aren't they cute?

32
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:35,940
Hina Matsuri seems to be something girls
are happy about no matter how old they get.

33
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,440
Good morning.

34
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,440
Good morning.

35
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,100
Where's Ryotsu?

36
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:46,200
He went out on patrol,

37
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:50,320
Patrol He isn't slacking
off somewhere again, is he?

38
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:53,060
Ryo-chan has a weakness for festivals,
doesn't he?

39
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:55,600
Festival or not, today is Hina Matsuri.

40
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:59,100
It has nothing to do with a lump of a man like Ryotsu,
I suppose.

41
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,740
Who decided this?

42
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:06,960
So it was Ryotsu after all.

43
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:12,380
Well, this is really funny.

44
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:13,460
What is it, Chief?

45
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,900
A big discovery! Take a look.

46
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,300
Right here, look.

47
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,800
March 3rd?

48
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:22,760
Ryo-chan's

49
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:25,360
birthday, which means it's today!

50
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,700
That means...

51
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:30,460
Ryo-san's birthday is Hina Matsuri?

52
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,160
No way, that Ryo-chan...

53
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:38,620
That doesn't match his image at all.

54
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,840
Asking us not to laugh
at this is impossible.

55
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,440
Good morning, Chief.

56
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:57,080
I was out on patrol to keep
the local residents safe.

57
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:01,940
I see, I see. You took your police notebook with you,
of course?

58
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:04,920
Of course, I kept it safe in my pocket.

59
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:07,880
That's strange. Did I put it in this one?

60
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:10,500
Here, it fell out, you know.

61
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,420
Here you go.

62
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,460
Good boy. Be careful.

63
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:21,160
Now that I think about it,
wasn't today someone's birthday?

64
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,620
Uh-oh.

65
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,900
Who was it again?

66
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,000
Terai, was it?

67
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,820
My birthday is May 5th.

68
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:28,460
That's the boys' festival, isn't it?

69
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,000
That's a birthday fit for a man.

70
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,300
Hey, Ryotsu.

71
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:34,580
Well, yeah.

72
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:36,440
Reiko's birthday is, if I remember right,

73
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,960
July 7th.

74
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,009
Tanabata.

75
00:04:39,059 --> 00:04:42,358
That's nice and romantic, very girly.

76
00:04:42,408 --> 00:04:43,680
Hey, Ryotsu.

77
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:44,700
Yeah, yeah.

78
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,183
But you should be more girly,

79
00:04:47,233 --> 00:04:50,000
there are romantic days too. For example...

80
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,860
March 3rd...

81
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:59,420
You're going to say it's the Hina Festival!
Got it! My birthday's March 3rd anyway!

82
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:03,500
Is that so? I didn't know that.

83
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,560
You knew it.

84
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,900
There's no need to worry about it so much.

85
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:10,660
There are plenty of boys born on March 3rd,
you know.

86
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,600
It just didn't quite fit Ryo-chan's image.

87
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:16,060
I'm not bothered by it either.

88
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:22,900
Ever since I was a kid, every birthday
has brought me nothing but bad luck.

89
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:28,100
The first time was, yeah,
back in elementary school.

90
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:32,060
I was trying to make hina dolls
for a girl in the neighborhood

91
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,880
and was lining up cardboard
hina dolls on the stairs,

92
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:39,220
when I slipped and took a
horrible tumble down the stairs.

93
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:43,960
Then in middle school,
I drank shirozake and got smashed,

94
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:46,920
fell into the Sumida River,
and got swept all the way out to sea.

95
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,840
In high school,
a girl from the snooty class caught me,

96
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,000
and I got strung up and publicly denounced.

97
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:54,240
They blamed it all on me alone.

98
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,860
In the end, I wasn't even
invited to the Hina Matsuri party.

99
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:00,320
And whenever I gamble, I always lose big.

100
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,000
dropping a cucumber

101
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,020
then a crow attacks you there,
and you fall too,

102
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:09,500
dining and dashing gets you chased by dogs,

103
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,260
and you get caught by a pushy salesman,

104
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:13,500
my birthday is cursed!

105
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,900
I'm starting to lose all sympathy for you.

106
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:19,260
It's all your own fault, isn't it?

107
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,100
No matter what anyone says,

108
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,420
I absolutely hate March 3rd!

109
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:26,060
You don't need to worry so much.

110
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,200
You've just been unlucky until now.

111
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:29,200
That's right!

112
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,860
We're having a Hina Matsuri party
at the women's dormitory today,

113
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,380
and I'll invite you too,
Ryo-chan, as a special favor.

114
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:35,600
What party?

115
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,060
I'm going, I'm going, I'm definitely going!

116
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:39,840
I was actually told to invite only Kei-chan,

117
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,220
but you're just so pitiful.

118
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:45,960
There'll be a feast, right?

119
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,080
Of course there will.

120
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,420
We're also planning to order sushi,
Ryo-chan's favorite.

121
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:50,100
Yes!

122
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:52,200
Finally,
a chance to eat sushi again after so long.

123
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,640
Yes, Kameari Park Police Box speaking.

124
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:57,140
Yes.

125
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,600
Chief, at Mr. Kimura
Hajime's place in 4-chome,

126
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,600
an incident has occurred.

127
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,460
At that rich family's house?

128
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:05,180
Alright, let's go, Ryotsu!

129
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,520
Me too?

130
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,640
Yes, don't dawdle!

131
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,140
Please tell us, Chief.

132
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,640
After we were invited to the
women's dormitory party, too.

133
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,780
The sushi...

134
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:15,140
That's scary!

135
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:17,800
Ryo-chan really has no luck, does he?

136
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:22,540
Listen, put the safety of the citizens first

137
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:26,560
Whatever the crime, it's the police's
job to prevent it before it happens.

138
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,360
Understand, Ryotsu?

139
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,340
Hurry up and get over here!

140
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:33,710
Tch.

141
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:37,440
Even though we get to eat sushi,
my luck's still rotten as ever.

142
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,120
I bought the juice.

143
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:39,800
Thanks.

144
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,140
Did they have Tsubutsu Grape?

145
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:41,860
Yep, they had it.

146
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,860
What? The back of this place
is the women's dormitory!

147
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:47,180
Looks like the moon hasn't fallen yet, then.

148
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:49,880
Ryotsu, hurry up!

149
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,240
Yes, yes, coming right now!

150
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,360
Threatening letter

151
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:03,560
I'll take the Hina dolls you have.

152
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:06,780
Declaration of Resolve:
Phantom Hina Festival Coins

153
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:10,580
Is this the threatening letter?

154
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:11,780
That's right.

155
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:14,480
How could this look like a car sales flyer?

156
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:17,860
Anyone can see it's a genuine threatening letter,
isn't it?

157
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,100
And here law-abiding
citizens are in trouble!

158
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:23,540
So you're saying you won't help us?

159
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,600
N-no, nothing like that...

160
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:28,320
Ever since that came,
I've been worried sick.

161
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:30,500
I can't sleep a wink at night.

162
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,100
O-of course.

163
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:34,000
Whatever the crime,

164
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,260
preventing it before it
happens is the police's job.

165
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:36,740
Yes.

166
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:39,000
But stealing hina dolls?

167
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,320
What a bizarre phantom thief.

168
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:43,460
Could it be someone's prank?

169
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:44,300
Ryotsu

170
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:47,440
Well, when it comes to our hina dolls,

171
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,760
they're not just any ordinary things,
you know.

172
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,060
They're worth over 500 million yen!

173
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:55,080
500 million yen!

174
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,852
That painting over there is 200 million yen,

175
00:09:02,902 --> 00:09:05,720
and this sculpture cost
about 300 million yen.

176
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,800
Well, a bargain, I suppose.

177
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:10,320
Something like this is 200 or 300 million?

178
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:13,380
Terereree! You mustn't touch that!

179
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,860
Just look, only look.

180
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:18,100
So, these hina dolls that are the problem?

181
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:22,540
We commissioned them three years ago for our eldest daughter,
and they were finally completed.

182
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:26,940
This one is for our eldest son, Tamaru, and this
one is for our eldest daughter, Amari, right?

183
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:31,660
Tamaru and Amari The parents'
wishes are blatantly on display.

184
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:34,520
Please wait in this room.

185
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:45,440
It's a seven-tier hina display
set made by Heian Komachi Tamagorō.

186
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:53,120
Hey, the dazzling Living National Treasure Tamagorō's
traditional craftsmanship lives on in this order, right?

187
00:09:53,720 --> 00:10:01,540
The costumes, the Wajima lacquerware tools, and so on,
are all things that train you in professional manners and expertise.

188
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:11,460
The gold folding screen behind uses pure gold leaf, the eyes are rubies,
the headpieces are diamonds, and sapphires and emeralds are countless.

189
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,180
I'm starving!

190
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:23,531
Idiot! Even if you break one of these fans,

191
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:25,920
you couldn't pay for it on your salary!

192
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:27,720
I-I know that!

193
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:30,113
Haha, no need to worry.

194
00:10:30,163 --> 00:10:32,300
We'll keep a strict watch over them.

195
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:34,880
Really, I'm counting on you.

196
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:37,100
I've gotten so thirsty.

197
00:10:37,940 --> 00:10:41,560
Hey! Get the tea ready!
The usual gyokuro with gold flakes!

198
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,540
Gyokuro with gold flakes?

199
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,880
Well, thank you.

200
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:47,520
What are you talking about?
I'm the one who's going to drink it.

201
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,720
It'd be a waste to serve tea to you lot.

202
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:53,680
I pay my taxes properly, Zakai.

203
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:55,860
If you're going to guard us for free,
that's not how it works.

204
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,400
Hey, I'm counting on you.

205
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:59,520
What a stingy bunch!

206
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,560
The party should be starting about now.

207
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,200
Ugh, b-Chief, I'm sorry.

208
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,340
I'm just going to step away to the restroom.

209
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,920
Toilet paper is limited to 10 centimeters.

210
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,060
The women's dorm is right over there.

211
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:22,820
We can get back before the Chief notices.

212
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:26,040
Still, is this really the bathroom?

213
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:31,900
Did you invite that caveman
from Kameari too, senpai?

214
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,620
Super lame, chobe-riba, modern times!

215
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,120
That's right, that's right.

216
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:37,820
What's the harm?

217
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:40,660
Besides,
he says it's Ryo-chan's birthday today.

218
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:42,260
Please just put up with him.

219
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:46,200
But senpai got a security job,
so whether he can come or not...

220
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,660
How would I know that?

221
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:50,040
He pops up everywhere like a cockroach.

222
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:53,240
Yeah, you turn around and
he's suddenly right behind you.

223
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:55,820
Sorry I'm such a cockroach

224
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,660
Honestly, after seeing those
500 million yen hina dolls,

225
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,280
our stuff looks awfully shabby, doesn't it?

226
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,140
500 million yen?

227
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,360
What's your problem?
If you've got complaints, go buy your own!

228
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,180
That's right, that's right!

229
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:05,020
Quit yelling, quit yelling.

230
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,640
Alright, let's start the party!

231
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:10,780
Ryo-chan,
is it okay to leave security like that?

232
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:15,460
It's fine. What is this taste?
Are you two actually cooking properly?

233
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:16,460
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

234
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,660
This is good, delicious.

235
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:52,660


236
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,820
Don't mind me, thank you in advance.

237
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:57,420
Hey, Reiko! Is the sushi still not here?

238
00:12:57,420 --> 00:13:00,460
Just wait a little longer, we ordered a lot.

239
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:02,900
You ate that much, and you still have room?

240
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:07,340
Sushi goes into a different stomach.

241
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,280
What do you mean, a different stomach?

242
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:12,420
Is your stomach a garbage chute?

243
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:16,000
If it weren't for Senior Reiko's request,
the worst.

244
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,360
If the Chief doesn't catch us like this,

245
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:25,480
March 3rd this year looks like
it's going to be a good day

246
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,560
Yes, it's me, it's Ryotsu.

247
00:13:31,180 --> 00:13:32,660
It's not me.

248
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:34,280
Yes, this is Ohara.

249
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,640
Chief Ohara.

250
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:39,120
Yes, yes, President, please don't worry.

251
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,960
We're checking thoroughly right now.

252
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:43,540
Yes, there are no abnormalities.

253
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:45,460
I'm worried about Ryotsu.

254
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,900
Yes, well, I'll make sure to
give him a proper talking-to.

255
00:13:48,140 --> 00:13:50,680
He's actually useful at times like this,
you know.

256
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:51,160
Yes.

257
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:54,000
Yes, this is Ryotsu.

258
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,420
It's Ohara. Are you still in the restroom?

259
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:59,140
Yes, I still can't get everything out.

260
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:02,080
What are you doing, Ryotsu, Kankichi?

261
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:04,960
What? Is someone there?

262
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:06,520
No, it's nothing.

263
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:09,160
If you're on duty, come back quickly.

264
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:10,260
Who's there, Ryotsu?

265
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:10,900
Shut up!

266
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,700
What? Wait there, I'm coming now.

267
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,660
No, no, you don't have to come.

268
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,900
What are we going to do, senpai?

269
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:20,360
Let's go back for now.

270
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,880
Save some sushi for me.

271
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,060
What is that guy doing?

272
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:29,520
Ouch, it hurts.

273
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,720
I ate too much and my stomach...

274
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,700
Ryotsu, are you in there?

275
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:43,480
Ryotsu!

276
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,680
Ryotsu!

277
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:46,680
Uh-oh.

278
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,340
Ryotsu!

279
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:51,900
Ryotsu, come out already!

280
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:56,680
Sorry, sorry.

281
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,760
You see, it's been a whole week,
Translation>
since I last went.

282
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:01,600
Considering how much I've
let out after a whole week,

283
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,540
it's really sticking out, isn't it?

284
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:04,220
Well, you know...

285
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:08,000
I'm off to guard the hina dolls now.

286
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:09,360
Excuse me, excuse me.

287
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:13,560
So this is the restroom?

288
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,180
Close call, close call.

289
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:27,420
That look means he's completely suspicious.

290
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:33,220
Hina dolls worth 500 million yen

291
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:36,640
Spending that much money on hina dolls,
the nerve of them.

292
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,380
Even hina dolls folded out of paper,

293
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,200
if they're made with heart,

294
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,440
that's good enough.

295
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:44,260
Besides, if you display something like this,

296
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,760
it's a big hassle.

297
00:15:57,860 --> 00:16:00,160
Gone, gone, gone, gone!

298
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:01,100
Gone!

299
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:06,680
Oh no, oh no, this is bad!

300
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:13,400
Even if just one of them goes missing,
and one more goes missing, and one more...

301
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:16,820
Huh? One, two, three... Let's see

302
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,000
20 million yen.

303
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,440
There's no way we can ever pay that back,
damn it.

304
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:25,620
Did they get hit while we
were at the women's dorm?

305
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:32,620
That's right!
The ones at the women's dorm...

306
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:37,900
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

307
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,960
I-I-I'm going to the restroom!

308
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,440
What, again?

309
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:48,980
I wonder if he'll really come back,
Ryo-chan.

310
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,860
And the sushi finally arrived, too.

311
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:52,480
Let's just leave him be.

312
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,100
Yeah, exactly.

313
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,540
Chomerik

314
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:57,380
It looks delicious.

315
00:16:57,380 --> 00:17:03,040
What's this?

316
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,420
It looks like insecticide.

317
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:10,920
It's fine.

318
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:11,400
Are you okay?

319
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,540
Sushi!

320
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:18,040
This comes first right now.

321
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,120
You're fired!

322
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:34,200
Who's there?

323
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:35,020
Ryo-chan?

324
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:44,300
As long as nobody touches them,
it'll be fine, right?

325
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:47,160
He's a stingy one,
so he'll never let anyone touch them.

326
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:48,340
Ryotsu

327
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:50,880
What are you doing?

328
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:51,060
Yes.

329
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:54,480
I'm really worried you can't handle this.

330
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,980
I'll take over here.

331
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:57,240
But

332
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,440
You're just the type.

333
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:03,140
Hearing about the authority, you might
secretly swap the evacuation dolls for fakes.

334
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:05,340
Absolutely not!

335
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:10,320
Besides, with that face of yours watching over them,
the evacuation dolls would be frightened.

336
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:11,320
Don't be ridiculous!

337
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:12,660
Just go already!

338
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:14,480
Fine, I-I understand.

339
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,300
They won't notice, right?

340
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,980
Yeah, looking at them like this,
they really are top-class masterpieces,

341
00:18:28,030 --> 00:18:29,120
the craftsmanship is on another level.

342
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:31,300
Please let them not notice.

343
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:33,280
They're truly a feast for the eyes.

344
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,940
Especially this Mebina,
she has a lovely face.

345
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:38,640
Don't stare at me like that,
you're embarrassing me.

346
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:43,760
What is this?

347
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,560
Oh no.

348
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,000
Damn, we've been found out.

349
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:05,140
We've done something terrible.

350
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:06,680
He thinks he did it himself.

351
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:08,540
At this point,

352
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:12,440
Chief...

353
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:15,620
What are you doing in a place like that?

354
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:20,340
No way.

355
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:25,160
Chief, you're a terrifying person.

356
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:29,080
I only touched it a little, sorry.

357
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:31,740
That's 500 million yen, 500 million!

358
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,780
That one eye alone is 50 million.

359
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:37,900
Well, after all,
she's the leading lady of the hina dolls.

360
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,280
What happened?

361
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,620
F-female doll's...

362
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:51,840
Such a heartless thing!

363
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:55,260
I'm terribly sorry, Mr. Kanakai Ichi.

364
00:19:56,280 --> 00:20:00,980
I will repay this debt without fail,
even if it takes my whole life.

365
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:05,400
You can say that all your life, but even working 24 hours a day,
you'd never pay it off, you know.

366
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:08,660
Your wife will have to work too,
and your daughter as well.

367
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:15,240
Poor Chief. Because of one man's mistake,
the Ohara family is ruined.

368
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,440
I understand.

369
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:22,000
As police officers who are supposed to protect citizens' property,
we've gone and done something this outrageous...

370
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:24,040
This is unforgivable.

371
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:29,060
I, Ohara, will take responsibility
and resign from the police force today.

372
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:31,540
I'll pay for the damage
with my retirement allowance.

373
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:33,611
No um,

374
00:20:33,661 --> 00:20:36,420
Chief, you don't have to go that far.

375
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,820
Don't stop me, Ryotsu.

376
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,720
That severance pay won't
come close to covering it.

377
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,620
Wait, no hold on a second.

378
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:46,440
Then I'll sell my house if I
have to and pay every last yen.

379
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:51,060
Mister, are you going to lose your house?

380
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:53,700
It can't be helped.

381
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:56,460
Little girl, it was my fault.

382
00:20:56,460 --> 00:21:01,240
When you make a mistake, it's only right
to apologize honestly and make amends.

383
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:06,100
Running away without taking responsibility
is the worst thing you can do.

384
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,660
Chief, actually, it was me.

385
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:16,620
Ryo-san,
don't you cause everyone any more trouble!

386
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:21,300
Then I'll go submit my resignation
to the station right away.

387
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,320
I'm sorry.

388
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,500
I'm sorry.

389
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,400
What's going on?

390
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:33,160
We were playing in this room...

391
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:36,380
This way, this way!

392
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:36,980
Wait.

393
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:45,780
We broke the hina doll.

394
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:50,180
Because we thought we'd get scolded.

395
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,800
So we wrote a confession

396
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:54,560
and tried to make it look
like a thief stole it.

397
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,600
W-what?

398
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,260
I'm sorry.

399
00:21:58,260 --> 00:22:01,920
We broke the hina doll Daddy treasured...

400
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,000
I'm sorry.

401
00:22:03,420 --> 00:22:05,060
Daddy, Daddy...

402
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:21,960
No one got hurt,

403
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:23,040
thank goodness no one got hurt.

404
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:26,840
Whose hina doll is this, anyway?

405
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:29,560
Didn't we make it from leftover scraps?

406
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:30,180
Hey,

407
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:30,780
Dad,

408
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:32,720
don't worry about it.

409
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:34,459
More than any doll,

410
00:22:34,509 --> 00:22:37,600
what I cherish most is you two.

411
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:40,940
Daddy, Daddy, I'm sorry!

412
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,220
Daddy, I'm sorry!

413
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:43,780
There, there.

414
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:46,880
But hiding it isn't right.

415
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:49,356
Just as this lady says,

416
00:22:49,406 --> 00:22:51,860
the best thing is to
honestly apologize, right?

417
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:53,020
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

418
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:54,320
Meow,

419
00:22:54,370 --> 00:22:57,840
So it all ends happily, Chief.

420
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:02,800
But then what about
these hina dolls over here?

421
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:03,220
Gulp.

422
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:04,680
No way.

423
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:06,400
Oh no.

424
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:08,720
No, that's

425
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:11,340
I just borrowed them from
the women's dorm for a bit.

426
00:23:11,340 --> 00:23:15,680
You knew the one I broke was a fake?

427
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:17,080
Well, that's

428
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:20,980
Mom

429
00:23:20,980 --> 00:23:21,860
Ahhhhhh

430
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:23,960
Ahhhhhh

431
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:36,460
Aaaah, I'm sorry, I did it. If I apologize honestly,
then those kids of mine...

432
00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:40,160
You'll work with me to pay it back. Got it?

433
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:49,040
Please work him to the bone.
Lucky you, Ryo-san... Chief, don't say that!

434
00:23:50,980 --> 00:23:53,280
Just as I thought,
nothing good ever happens on March 3rd.

435
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:54,520
Damn it!

436
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:58,340
I hate Hina Matsuri!

437
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:07,740
Deep in the mountains of Thailand
stands a castle no one knows of.

438
00:24:07,740 --> 00:24:09,560
It is called the Phantom Castle.

439
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:11,820
On its summit sit a pair of golden shachi,

440
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:13,960
their golden scales glittering.

441
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:17,780
Yosh! I'll take those golden shachi!

442
00:24:17,780 --> 00:24:20,600
Next time: Ninja vs. Indi-Ryos!

443
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:21,680
See you next time.

444
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:32,700
Even if you try to stop the clock,

445
00:24:34,380 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps on passing.

446
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:42,720
Don't keep that sour face,

447
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:48,000
let's laugh it off and live on.

448
00:24:50,300 --> 00:24:57,900
Even if today it's raining,

449
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:03,460
tomorrow it'll be sunny.

450
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave our hands.

451
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,860
Unpleasant things, goodbye.

452
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's try living the way we like.

453
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,960
Good things will come.

454
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:30,220
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

455
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

